//! A univariate polynomial commitment scheme backed by WHIR.
//!
//! `p3-whir` is a multilinear scheme, while `p3_uni_stark::StarkGenericConfig`
//! wants a univariate one. This adapter commits each matrix column by its
//! coefficient vector — read as a multilinear's hypercube evaluations — and
//! turns every univariate opening into the equality claim
//! [`crate::pcs::whir::uni::bridge::univariate_eq_point`] derives.
//!
//! One WHIR argument covers one commitment. The univariate interface hands the
//! prover several commitments per opening, so a proof carries one WHIR argument
//! per commitment, replayed in order against a shared transcript.
//!
//! # Zero knowledge
//!
//! This adapter is a *hiding* PCS: [`UnivariateStarkPcs::ZK`] is `true`, so the
//! uni-stark and batch-stark provers run every blinding branch that a
//! non-hiding PCS leaves dead. Three masks make a proof zero knowledge, all drawn
//! from the instance's [`StdRng`]:
//!
//! 1. **Trace interleaving** ([`WhirUniPcs::commit`]). Each `N x w` trace
//!    becomes `2N x w` with the real rows on the even indices and random rows
//!    between them. Because the real rows sit on the subgroup generated by
//!    `g_N = g_{2N}^2`, the randomized trace polynomial `T'` agrees with the
//!    real trace on that whole coset, so every AIR constraint still vanishes
//!    there and `Q' = C'/Z_H` remains a polynomial. Off that coset — which is
//!    exactly where the quotient domain lives — `T'` is random, so the quotient
//!    values the prover opens carry no information about the witness.
//! 2. **Quotient chunk masking** ([`WhirUniPcs::get_quotient_ldes`]). Each
//!    chunk `q_i` on domain `D_i` becomes `q_i + Z_{D_i} * T_i` for random
//!    `T_i`. The recomposition identity `L_i(X) * Z_{D_i}(X) = cis_i * P(X)`
//!    (with `P = prod_j Z_{D_j}` and `cis_i = 1 / prod_{j != i} Z_{D_j}(first_i)`)
//!    turns the verifier's recomposed quotient into
//!    `Q + P * sum_i cis_i T_i`, so forcing `sum_i cis_i T_i = 0` on the last
//!    chunk leaves the recomposed value untouched while making every opened
//!    chunk value uniformly random.
//! 3. **The R commitment** ([`WhirUniPcs::get_opt_randomization_poly_commitment`]).
//!    A random `2N x DIMENSION` matrix, committed before the trace challenge and
//!    opened at the out-of-domain point, so the opened trace values are masked by
//!    something the verifier cannot predict when it samples.
//!
//! Hiding holds only if `rng` is cryptographically secure; the seed comes from
//! the OS entropy source at construction time. Private prover data may be opened
//! **once**, including across clones — [`Clone`] forks the RNG stream so a clone
//! never reproduces the original masks, but re-opening the same prover data
//! would pair two openings of one mask and is rejected. Recommit for another
//! proof. This restriction does not apply to public preprocessing.

